<h1>Stirling's approximation</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
For large values of n, <a href="factorial.html"><em>n!</em></a> &asymp; (n/e)<sup>n</sup> &radic;(2n&pi;).
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="factorial.html"><em>factorial</em></a>, <a href="gammaFunction.html"><em>gamma function</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
This approximation is taken directly from <a href="stirlingsFormula.html"><em>Stirling's formula</em></a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
Peter Luschny lists and evaluates <a href="http://www.luschny.de/math/factorial/approx/SimpleCases.html" target="_blank">many approximation formulas for n!</a>. See Eric W. Weisstein, <a href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/StirlingsApproximation.html" target="_blank">Stirling's Approximation</a> for a derivation and other approximations.
</p>

